<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Engelbert Dollfuss</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1892–1934</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Engelbert Dollfuss was an Austrian Christian Social politician, chancellor from 1932. In March 1933 he suspended parliament and ruled by decree, banning the Communists and Austrian Nazis. After crushing the Social Democrats in the civil war of February 1934, he created the authoritarian Federal State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. He was murdered by Austrian Nazis during a failed coup in July 1934.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/engelbert-dollfuss.jpg" alt="Engelbert Dollfuss" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Engelbert_Dollfuss_1-E-652.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
